// Title: Suspicious VBScript UN2452 Pattern
// Sigma ID: 20c3f09d-c53d-4e85-8b74-6aa50e2f1b61
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2021-03-05 | Modified: 2022-10-09
// ATT&CK: privilege-escalation, persistence, T1547.001
// Tags: detection.emerging-threats
// Description: Detects suspicious inline VBScript keywords as used by UNC2452
// False positives:
//   - Unknown
// References:
//   - https://www.microsoft.com/security/blog/2021/03/04/goldmax-goldfinder-sibot-analyzing-nobelium-malware/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/05d1031f537e830b76da53bae2400c5814c89165/rules-emerging-threats/2020/TA/SolarWinds-Supply-Chain/proc_creation_win_apt_unc2452_vbscript_pattern.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where (ProcessCommandLine contains "Execute" and ProcessCommandLine contains "CreateObject" and ProcessCommandLine contains "RegRead" and ProcessCommandLine contains "window.close" and ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion") and (not(ProcessCommandLine contains "\\Software\\Microsoft\\Windows\\CurrentVersion\\Run"))
